   "text": {
    "source": "wikipedia",
    "title": "North Pacific hake",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Pacific_hake",
    "revision": "1358983544",
    "timestamp": "2026-06-12",
    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "about": "taxon",
    "extract": "The North Pacific hake, Pacific hake, Pacific whiting, or jack salmon is a ray-finned fish in the genus Merluccius, found in the northeast Pacific Ocean from northern Vancouver Island to the northern part of the Gulf of California. It is a silver-gray fish with black speckling, growing to a length of 90 cm (3 ft). It is a migratory offshore fish and undergoes a daily vertical migration from the surface to the seabed at depths down to about 1,000 m (3,300 ft).",
    "lead": "The North Pacific hake, Pacific hake, Pacific whiting, or jack salmon is a ray-finned fish in the genus Merluccius, found in the northeast Pacific Ocean from northern Vancouver Island to the northern part of the Gulf of California. It is a silver-gray fish with black speckling, growing to a length of 90 cm (3 ft)."
   },
